 REQ-PB-091 Implement the 25-question Transformation Health Check with score and top 3 actions 
  PROC: Assessor answers all 25 questions; score out of 25 is calculated; three top actions are required; reassessments tracked 
  NOTES: Playbook (B0149, B0150, B0161): the 25 questions (checkboxes), 'Score: __ / 25' and 'Top 3 actions'. Master-prompt additions (§14 M0262, M0288): Yes=1/No=0 scoring (REQ-S14-001) and incomplete-assessment handling (REQ-S14-002), both implementation assumption D-010 (M0262); the top three improvement actions are required and reassessments are tracked over time (M0288). Interpretations: the requirement for three actions is enforced by rejecting submission of an assessment with fewer than three.

 REQ-PB-092 Interpret the health-check score with the four source bands 
  PROC: Completed assessments show the band text matching the score 
  NOTES: Playbook (B0151, B0152): the four score bands and their text. Master-prompt additions: none; §14 M0288 restates the four bands (its top-three-actions and reassessment clause is covered by REQ-PB-091). Interpretations: none.

 REQ-PB-093 Let methodology administrators configure the default T06 weight set and scoring rubrics in Playbook Studio as versioned configuration 
  PROC: A methodology admin edits the default weight set and the 1-5 rubric descriptors in a Studio draft; publishing applies the 100% rule and creates an immutable version, which becomes the starting weight set and rubric of transformations created afterwards; existing transformations keep their pinned weight set and rubric until a deliberate migration 
  NOTES: Playbook (B0077): weights are adjusted to the transformation context. Master-prompt additions (§9 M0176; §6 M0154, M0155): scoring rubrics and approved weights are configurable and versioned, administered in Playbook Studio with draft, publish and version pinning; the source weights 25/25/20/15/15 are seeded (M0176, REQ-PB-048). Interpretations: that seed is the initial Studio default for new transformations, and ADM configures defaults only, never approving a transformation's weights (permissions-matrix.md §5 rule 2). AN-05: split from REQ-PB-049 (finding F-DG0-001).

 REQ-PB-048 Apply T06 default weights 25/25/20/15/15 with a 1-5 scale and a calculated weighted score 
  PROC: Weighted score = sum(score x weight) on the 1-5 scale; scores outside 1-5 rejected; missing score marks the row incomplete 
  NOTES: Playbook (B0076): the weights 25/25/20/15/15, the 1-5 scale and a calculated weighted score. Master-prompt additions (§9 M0176): weighted score = sum(score × weight), giving a 1-5 result, and a missing score means incomplete, not zero. Interpretations: none.
