== REQ-PB-042 B0063;M0147 | Support the TOM canvas workshop and convert unresolved items into design decisions with owners
 IN: Workshop date;Duration (90-120 minutes);Business owner participants;Agenda;Contributions;Unresolved items;Resulting design decision or action;Owner
 PROC: Facilitator publishes an agenda and runs a workshop session with business owners, capturing contributions per dimension; each unresolved item is converted in one action into a T04 design decision with owner (source) or an owned action (extension)
 ACC: A01: converting an unresolved item creates a T04 row linked to the workshop with owner set; an item without an owner cannot be converted; converting an item to an action creates an owned action linked to the workshop; the workshop cannot be closed while unresolved items remain unconverted
 NOTES: Source-grounded core (cited B blocks). AN-04 consolidation: absorbs former REQ-S05-004 (Run the facilitated 90-120-minute TOM workshop mode with agenda, captured contributions and conversion of unresolved items into decisions or actions); its anchors M0147 and acceptance are carried here. The agenda, per-dimension contribution capture, conversion into actions and the no-close-with-unconverted-items rule are master prompt §5 additions (M0147), not playbook content; the 90-120-minute workshop with business owners and conversion into design decisions with owners is source (B0063).

== REQ-PB-058 B0088;M0173 | Prevent double counting: each benefit has a unique owner, baseline, formula and financial-statement or non-financial KPI link
 IN: Benefit ID;Owner;Baseline;Formula;Financial statement line or non-financial KPI;Parent benefit;Shared-benefit group;Contribution allocation
 PROC: System rejects a benefit without a single owner, baseline, formula and a financial statement line or agreed non-financial KPI; initiatives link to canonical benefits via allocations, parent/child relationships and shared-benefit groups; portfolio totals sum canonical benefits, not links, so a shared benefit rolls up once
 ACC: A10: a benefit with two owners is rejected; a 10 million SAR benefit shared by two initiatives appears once (10 million SAR) in the portfolio total
 NOTES: Shared-benefit allocation rules detailed in master prompt §8. AN-04 consolidation: absorbs former REQ-S08-012 (Prevent double counting through a canonical benefit register, parent/child relationships, shared-benefit groups and contribution allocations so portfolio aggregation counts a shared benefit once); its anchors M0173 and acceptance are carried here. The canonical benefit register, parent/child relationships, shared-benefit groups and contribution allocations are the master prompt §8 mechanism (M0173); the unique owner, baseline, formula and statement/KPI link is source (B0088). Allocation limits: REQ-S08-013; overlap warnings: REQ-S08-014.

== REQ-PB-069 B0105;M0216 | Manage adoption as an outcome with measurable leading indicators, separate from delivery
 IN: Adoption outcome;Adoption KPI;Adoption trajectory;Adoption actual;Intervention;Owner
 PROC: Adoption has its own outcome, KPIs and status distinct from initiative delivery status; adoption KPIs use trajectories, and a gap beyond threshold creates one intervention with owner
 ACC: A11: an initiative with delivery Complete and adoption below trajectory shows adoption at risk and triggers an intervention; an adoption actual below trajectory creates exactly one intervention
 NOTES: Source-grounded core (cited B blocks). AN-04 consolidation: absorbs former REQ-S11-003 (Track adoption actuals against adoption trajectories and create corrective interventions when gaps appear); its anchors M0216 and acceptance are carried here. Trajectory-based adoption tracking and the exactly-one-intervention rule are master prompt §11 additions (M0216); adoption as an outcome with leading indicators, separate from delivery, is source (B0105). Indicators: REQ-PB-071/072.
